Frequently asked questions

Which languages do you translate?

We translate between English, French, German, Spanish, Italian and Dutch, among other languages. If you need a different language, ask us and we will tell you what is possible. Your translator works into their native language.

Can you translate between two non-English languages?

Yes, we can translate directly between many European language pairs. Direct translation avoids the errors that come from going through English first. Tell us the pair and we will confirm the best route.

Do you handle several languages in one project?

Yes, we can manage a project in many languages at once and keep it organised. You get one contact and one set of deadlines. Share your language list and we will plan the work with you.

Can you translate regional variants such as Latin American Spanish?

Yes, tell us the country or region your readers live in. Your translator then chooses the vocabulary and style that suit that audience. This matters for marketing, legal and customer-facing texts.

How do you choose the translator for each language?

We choose a native speaker of the target language with experience in your subject. A second linguist reviews the result for accuracy and style. You can tell us if you prefer to work with the same linguist again.
